{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R3tVmUnqhvasEU9WfWuAnq","type":"tool_result","content":"38:[Omitted long matching line]\n94:| Namespaced vs cluster-scoped | Deployments/Services are namespaced; Nodes, PersistentVolumes, StorageClasses, and namespaces themselves are not. |\n103:| What Kubernetes provides | Service discovery/load balancing, storage orchestration, automated rollouts/rollbacks, automatic bin packing, self-healing, secret & config management, batch execution, horizontal scaling, IPv4/IPv6 dual-stack, extensibility. |\n205:| Secret storage default | Secrets are stored **unencrypted** in etcd by default; encryption at rest must be enabled explicitly. |\n232:### D2.4 — Storage\n236:| PersistentVolume (PV) | A piece of cluster storage, admin-provisioned or dynamically provisioned; a cluster resource like a node. |\n238:| PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) | A user's *request* for storage — a specific size and access mode. |\n240:| StorageClass | The resource letting admins offer PV varieties (performance tiers etc.) without exposing implementation. |\n241:| Static provisioning | An admin pre-creates PVs carrying real storage details. |\n242:| Dynamic provisioning | The cluster creates a PV on demand for a PVC that requests a StorageClass configured for it. |\n243:| Disabling dynamic provisioning | A claim requesting storage class `\"\"` opts itself out of dynamic provisioning. |\n249:| Delete | Removes both the PV object and the backing storage asset; the **default for dynamically-provisioned volumes** (inherited from the StorageClass). |\n255:| StatefulSet + PV | The pairing that gives stateful workloads durable per-Pod storage. |\n323:| Pull model | Prometheus scrapes metrics over HTTP; each server is standalone with no distributed-storage dependency. |\n382:| Former TAGs (pre-2025) | App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage. |\n385:| SIG orientations | Vertical (Network, Storage, Node), horizontal (Scalability, Architecture), or project-support (Testing, Release, Docs). |\n454:| StorageClass · dynamic provisioning · reclaim policy | PV, PVC, binding |\n487:4. **Storage (D2.4) must precede StatefulSet's full treatment.** Either introduce StatefulSet lightly in the workloads chapter and return to it after PV/PVC, or place storage before the deep workloads pass. The former is better for the reader — StatefulSet belongs with its siblings.\n517:| 14 | \"Everything lives in a namespace.\" | Nodes, PersistentVolumes, StorageClasses — and namespace objects themselves — are not namespaced. | [source] |\n572:| 64 | Reversing PV and PVC. | PV = the **supply** (a piece of cluster storage). PVC = the **demand** (a user's request). Pods reference PVCs, never PVs. | [source] |\n574:| 66 | \"Deleting a PVC always keeps the data.\" | Dynamically-provisioned volumes inherit the StorageClass reclaim policy, which **defaults to Delete** — removing both the PV object and the backing storage asset. | [source] |\n577:| 69 | \"Requesting storage class `\"\"` uses the default class.\" | The empty string **disables dynamic provisioning** for that claim. | [source] |\n613:| 95 | \"Prometheus needs distributed storage / clustered backends.\" | Each server is **standalone and autonomous**, deliberately, so it works when the rest of your infrastructure is broken. | [source] |\n629:| 111 | Using the pre-2025 TAG list. | TAGs were **restructured in 2025**. Current: Developer Experience, Infrastructure, Operational Resilience, Security and Compliance, Workloads Foundation. The old list (App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage) appears throughout older study material. | [source] |\n654:| G11 | **CNI, CSI, and CRI as the three pluggable interfaces.** CRI is covered; CNI is implied (\"network plugin\"); CSI is entirely absent. The three-interface story is core cloud-native-architecture framing. | D2.1, D2.4, D1.4, D4.2 | kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/compute-storage-net/ + the CNI and CSI specs |\n655:| G12 | **Volume types other than PV/PVC**: emptyDir, hostPath, configMap/secret volumes, projected, ephemeral. A large share of real Pod storage and not covered. | D2.4 | kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/ |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd121258-654c-4cd3-a647-6717d19a05eb","uuid":"173e09e8-530d-4f8e-b11b-dfaba7c7484f","timestamp":"2026-08-25T09:06:31.540Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"38:[Omitted long matching line]\n94:| Namespaced vs cluster-scoped | Deployments/Services are namespaced; Nodes, PersistentVolumes, StorageClasses, and namespaces themselves are not. |\n103:| What Kubernetes provides | Service discovery/load balancing, storage orchestration, automated rollouts/rollbacks, automatic bin packing, self-healing, secret & config management, batch execution, horizontal scaling, IPv4/IPv6 dual-stack, extensibility. |\n205:| Secret storage default | Secrets are stored **unencrypted** in etcd by default; encryption at rest must be enabled explicitly. |\n232:### D2.4 — Storage\n236:| PersistentVolume (PV) | A piece of cluster storage, admin-provisioned or dynamically provisioned; a cluster resource like a node. |\n238:| PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) | A user's *request* for storage — a specific size and access mode. |\n240:| StorageClass | The resource letting admins offer PV varieties (performance tiers etc.) without exposing implementation. |\n241:| Static provisioning | An admin pre-creates PVs carrying real storage details. |\n242:| Dynamic provisioning | The cluster creates a PV on demand for a PVC that requests a StorageClass configured for it. |\n243:| Disabling dynamic provisioning | A claim requesting storage class `\"\"` opts itself out of dynamic provisioning. |\n249:| Delete | Removes both the PV object and the backing storage asset; the **default for dynamically-provisioned volumes** (inherited from the StorageClass). |\n255:| StatefulSet + PV | The pairing that gives stateful workloads durable per-Pod storage. |\n323:| Pull model | Prometheus scrapes metrics over HTTP; each server is standalone with no distributed-storage dependency. |\n382:| Former TAGs (pre-2025) | App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage. |\n385:| SIG orientations | Vertical (Network, Storage, Node), horizontal (Scalability, Architecture), or project-support (Testing, Release, Docs). |\n454:| StorageClass · dynamic provisioning · reclaim policy | PV, PVC, binding |\n487:4. **Storage (D2.4) must precede StatefulSet's full treatment.** Either introduce StatefulSet lightly in the workloads chapter and return to it after PV/PVC, or place storage before the deep workloads pass. The former is better for the reader — StatefulSet belongs with its siblings.\n517:| 14 | \"Everything lives in a namespace.\" | Nodes, PersistentVolumes, StorageClasses — and namespace objects themselves — are not namespaced. | [source] |\n572:| 64 | Reversing PV and PVC. | PV = the **supply** (a piece of cluster storage). PVC = the **demand** (a user's request). Pods reference PVCs, never PVs. | [source] |\n574:| 66 | \"Deleting a PVC always keeps the data.\" | Dynamically-provisioned volumes inherit the StorageClass reclaim policy, which **defaults to Delete** — removing both the PV object and the backing storage asset. | [source] |\n577:| 69 | \"Requesting storage class `\"\"` uses the default class.\" | The empty string **disables dynamic provisioning** for that claim. | [source] |\n613:| 95 | \"Prometheus needs distributed storage / clustered backends.\" | Each server is **standalone and autonomous**, deliberately, so it works when the rest of your infrastructure is broken. | [source] |\n629:| 111 | Using the pre-2025 TAG list. | TAGs were **restructured in 2025**. Current: Developer Experience, Infrastructure, Operational Resilience, Security and Compliance, Workloads Foundation. The old list (App Delivery, Contributor Strategy, Environmental Sustainability, Network, Observability, Runtime, Security, Storage) appears throughout older study material. | [source] |\n654:| G11 | **CNI, CSI, and CRI as the three pluggable interfaces.** CRI is covered; CNI is implied (\"network plugin\"); CSI is entirely absent. The three-interface story is core cloud-native-architecture framing. | D2.1, D2.4, D1.4, D4.2 | kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/extend-kubernetes/compute-storage-net/ + the CNI and CSI specs |\n655:| G12 | **Volume types other than PV/PVC**: emptyDir, hostPath, configMap/secret volumes, projected, ephemeral. A large share of real Pod storage and not covered. | D2.4 | kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/ |","numLines":26,"totalLines":26}}
